Upgraded the `toml` crate from 0.5 to 1.x. Node configuration parse errors are now rendered over several lines: the position, the offending line, then the cause. TOML 1.1 syntax (multi-line inline tables, trailing commas in inline tables, `\e` and `\xHH` string escapes) and integers above `i64::MAX` in unsigned fields are now accepted. A DEL character (0x7F) inside a comment is now rejected, so the node and the signer refuse to start until it is removed.
The signer now prints configuration loading errors to stderr and exits with status 1 instead of panicking. Parse errors carry the parser's rendered message (line, column and the offending line) instead of the debug representation of the error.
